-- title:
--   Level equation transports along a correspondence of rigidifications
-- statement:
--   The setting is the one used throughout the Čerednik–Drinfeld part of the development, and the hypotheses fall into the following groups.
--
--   **Numerical data and the base ring.** Primes $r$ and $\bar r$ with $\bar r \neq r$, a natural number $N$ with $N \neq 0$ and $r \nmid N$. A characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal O$ which is a discrete valuation ring with irreducible element $\pi$, complete for the $(\pi)$-adic topology, whose residue ring $\mathcal O/(\pi)$ has exactly $r$ elements and in which $(r) = (\pi)$; together with a characteristic-zero fraction field $K_0$ of $\mathcal O$.
--
--   **The unramified lift.** A characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra, with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$, such that $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ is complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$, that ideal is maximal, every element of $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ satisfies a monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo it (`hOnr_alg`), every monic polynomial of positive degree over $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ has a root modulo it (`hOnr_closed`), and $\mathrm{Fr}(x) \equiv x^{r}$ modulo it for all $x$ (`hFr`).
--
--   **The quaternion algebra and its order.** Rationals $a, b$ such that $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ satisfies `IsIndefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b r rbar`, i.e. $0 < a$ or $0 < b$, and for every finite place $v$ of $\mathbb Q$ every nonzero element of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b] \otimes_{\mathbb Q} \mathbb Q_v$ is a unit precisely when $v$ divides $r$ or $\bar r$. A $\mathbb Z$-submodule $\Lambda$ which is a maximal order (an order maximal among orders containing it) and contains every rational integer; and a map $\mathrm{coord} \colon \Lambda \to \mathbb{Z}_{r^2} \times \mathbb{Z}_{r^2}$ (where $\mathbb{Z}_{r^2}$ denotes the Witt vectors of $\mathbb F_{r^2}$) which is an order coordinate in the sense of `IsOrderCoord`: additive, injective, sending $1$ to $(1,0)$, satisfying the Frobenius-twisted multiplication rule, dense modulo all powers of $r$, and compatible with reduced traces.
--
--   **Data in the residue characteristic.** A fake elliptic curve $A_0$ for $(\Lambda, N)$ over $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(\pi)$, a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $X_0$ over that ring of height $4$, two-dimensional formal coordinates $\theta_0$ for $A_0.f$, and the hypothesis that $A_0$ is a formal module via $\mathrm{coord}$, $X_0$, $\theta_0$ (the coordinates are formal coordinates for the relative group law, and the $\Lambda$-action on sections is computed by the series $\mathrm{coord}$ prescribes).
--
--   **The special formal module and the moduli package.** A ring homomorphism $\iota \colon \mathbb{Z}_{r^2} \to \mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}$; a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $\Phi$ over $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(r)$ which is special with respect to $\iota$ followed by reduction and has height $4$; a moduli package $M$ over $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ which is a Zariski sheaf; a family $\eta$ assigning to each ring $B$ with a ring map $\psi$ from $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ and $r$ nilpotent in $B$ a map from $\Phi$-rigidified objects over $B$ to $M(B,\psi)$; and the three-part hypothesis `hη` stating that over noetherian bases $\eta$ separates admissible rigidified objects exactly up to isomorphism, is compatible with base change along ring maps over $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}$, and is locally surjective, every point of $M$ becoming of the form $\eta(t)$ with $t$ admissible after passing to the members of a finite affine cover. Further, an injective ring homomorphism $E_0$ from the centraliser of $\{\Phi.\mathrm{actEnd}\,a\} \cup \{\Phi.\mathrm{varpiEnd}\}$ into $M_2(K_0)$, together with a natural number $m$ such that $r^{m}A$ lies in the image of $E_0$ for every $A \in M_2(\mathcal O)$ and $r^{m}E_0(e)$ lies in $M_2(\mathcal O)$ for every $e$ (`hE₀`).
--
--   **Comparison of the two reductions.** A ring map $\kappa \colon \mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(\pi) \to \mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(r)$ commuting with the two quotient maps, a natural number $n_0$ and a series $\beta_0$ which is an isogeny of height $4n_0$ from $\Phi$ to $X_0$ pushed forward along $\kappa$.
--
--   **Level structure and the base.** A natural number $n$ with $r \nmid n$ and a full level-$n$ structure $P_0$ on $A_0$ (a section of $A_0.f$ over the identity killed by $n$, generating the geometric $n$-torsion under $\Lambda$, with the prescribed annihilator condition). A noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$, an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\psi \colon \mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}} \to B$, and the hypothesis that the image of $\pi$ in $B$ is nilpotent.
--
--   **Two curves, an isomorphism and a correspondence.** Fake elliptic curves $E, E'$ for $(\Lambda,N)$ over $B$, an isomorphism $i \colon E.A \cong E'.A$ over $\mathrm{Spec}\,B$ (that is, $i_{\mathrm{hom}}$ followed by $E'.f$ equals $E.f$) which is an isomorphism via `IsoVia`: it respects the relative group laws, commutes with the $\Lambda$-actions, and matches the level subschemes in both directions. Rigidifications $\varrho$ of $E$ and $\varrho'$ of $E'$ relative to $A_0$ and $\psi$; each consists of a curve $E_b$ over $B/(\pi)$ pulling back $E$, a curve $A_b$ over $B/(\pi)$ pulling back $A_0$ along the residue leg of $\psi$, an exponent $d$, and an isogeny pair $(\varphi, \varphi')$ of degree $r^{d}$ between $E_b$ and $A_b$ preserving the level. A morphism $i_b \colon \varrho.E_b.A \to \varrho'.E_b.A$ with $i_b$ followed by $\varrho'.g_b$ equal to $\varrho.g_b$ followed by $i_{\mathrm{hom}}$, and $i_b$ followed by $\varrho'.E_b.f$ equal to $\varrho.E_b.f$; a morphism $u_A \colon \varrho'.A_b.A \to \varrho.A_b.A$ exhibiting $\varrho'.A_b$ as the pullback of $\varrho.A_b$ along the identity of $B/(\pi)$ (in the sense of `IsPullbackVia`: a pullback square compatible with the group laws, the $\Lambda$-actions and the level), with $u_A$ followed by $\varrho.g_A$ equal to $\varrho'.g_A$; and natural numbers $i_1, j_1$ with the correspondence identity `hcorr`
--   $$i_b \,;\, \varrho'.\varphi \,;\, u_A \,;\, \varrho.A_b.\mathrm{act}(r^{i_1}) \;=\; \varrho.\varphi \,;\, \varrho.A_b.\mathrm{act}(r^{j_1}),$$
--   where the actions are by the rational integers $r^{i_1}, r^{j_1} \in \Lambda$ and $;$ denotes composition in diagrammatic order. Full level-$n$ structures $P_n$ on $E$ and $P_n'$ on $E'$ with $P_n$ transported by $i_{\mathrm{hom}}$ equal to $P_n'$.
--
--   **The section $Q$ and the rigidified object $t$.** A morphism $Q \colon \mathrm{Spec}(B/(\pi)) \to \varrho.A_b.A$ which is a section of $\varrho.A_b.f$ and satisfies: $Q$ followed by $\varrho.g_A$ equals $\mathrm{Spec}$ of the residue leg of $\psi$ followed by the underlying morphism of $P_0$. A formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $X$ over $B$ and two-dimensional formal coordinates $\theta$ for $E.f$ making $E$ a formal module via $\mathrm{coord}$, $X$, $\theta$. A natural number $j \le 1$ and a $\Phi$-rigidified object $t$ over $B$ with $t.X = X$, admissible with respect to $\iota$ and the Frobenius twist $\mathrm{frobTwist}\,\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}\,\mathrm{Fr}\,(-j)\,\psi$ (that is, $t.X$ is special, of height $4$, and $t.\rho$ is an isogeny of height $4\,t.n$ from the reduction of $\Phi$ to the reduction of $t.X$); and the level equation `hlev`: the reduction modulo $(\pi)$ of the $r^{t.n}$-fold multiple of $P_n$ in the relative group law of $E$ equals $Q$ followed by $\varrho.\varphi'$ followed by $\varrho.g_b$.
--
--   **Formal expansion of the dual leg.** A ring map $\kappa_B \colon B/(\pi) \to B/(r)$ compatible with the two quotient maps, and compatible with $\kappa$ in the sense that $\kappa_B$ after the residue leg of $\psi$ equals the residue map of $\psi$ after $\kappa$. A series $\sigma$ over $B/(\pi)$ satisfying `hσ`: for every commutative ring $B''$ carrying algebra structures over $B/(\pi)$, over $B$ and over $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(\pi)$ such that the structure map from $B$ factors through reduction modulo $(\pi)$ and the structure map from $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(\pi)$ factors through the residue leg of $\psi$, for every ideal $J$ of $B''$ and every $m$ with $J^{m+1} = 0$, every pair $s$ of elements of $J$, and every morphism $P_A \colon \mathrm{Spec}\,B'' \to \varrho.A_b.A$ lying over the structure morphism and with $P_A$ followed by $\varrho.g_A$ equal to the section $\theta_0(B'',s)$, the composite of $P_A$ with $\varrho.\varphi'$ and $\varrho.g_b$ equals the section $\theta(B'', (\mathrm{nilEval}\,m\,(\sigma_i)\,s)_i)$, where $\mathrm{nilEval}$ evaluates the truncation of $\sigma_i$ at $s$. Finally `htρ`: $t.\rho$ is the composite of $\sigma$ pushed along $\kappa_B$ with $\beta_0$ pushed along the residue map of $\psi$, precomposed with the substitution $X_i \mapsto X_i^{\,r^{j}}$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** For every natural number $n'$ with
--   $$n' + (\varrho.d + j_1) \;=\; t.n + (\varrho'.d + i_1),$$
--   there exists a morphism $Q' \colon \mathrm{Spec}(B/(\pi)) \to \varrho'.A_b.A$ such that
--
--   1. $Q'$ followed by $\varrho'.A_b.f$ is the identity of $\mathrm{Spec}(B/(\pi))$, i.e. $Q'$ is a section;
--
--   2. $Q'$ followed by $\varrho'.g_A$ equals $\mathrm{Spec}$ of the residue leg of $\psi$ followed by the underlying morphism of $P_0$; and
--
--   3. the reduction modulo $(\pi)$ of the $r^{n'}$-fold multiple of $P_n'$ in the relative group law of $E'$ — that is, $\mathrm{Spec}$ of the quotient map $B \to B/(\pi)$ followed by the underlying morphism of $\mathrm{nsmulPt}\,E'.L\,\mathbf 1\,(r^{n'})\,P_n'$ — equals $Q'$ followed by $\varrho'.\varphi'$ followed by $\varrho'.g_b$.
--
--   This is the bookkeeping step which moves the height-normalised level equation from one rigidification to another across an isomorphism of fake elliptic curves matched by a correspondence of degree exponents $i_1, j_1$: the exponent $t.n$ of the source is replaced by the exponent $n'$ determined by $n' + (\varrho.d + j_1) = t.n + (\varrho'.d + i_1)$, and the section $Q$ of $\varrho.A_b$ by a section $Q'$ of $\varrho'.A_b$ inducing the same base level $P_0$. It is used in the proof of [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.FakeEllipticCurve.Rigidification.isNormLevelTransport_of_isoVia_of_corr_of_isFormalModuleVia`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.FakeEllipticCurve.Rigidification.isNormLevelTransport_of_isoVia_of_corr_of_isFormalModuleVia), and relies on [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.FakeEllipticCurve.pushPt_act_natCast_eq_nsmulPt`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.FakeEllipticCurve.pushPt_act_natCast_eq_nsmulPt) to identify the action of a rational integer on sections with the corresponding multiple in the relative group law.
